{"id":"7f1eff698d85f429504a56d3b9335ce54b5f40da","axis":"silent","repo":"systemd/systemd","sha":"7f1eff698d85f429504a56d3b9335ce54b5f40da","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"NEWS","lines":["@@ -94,8 +94,14 @@ CHANGES WITH 263 in spe:","           validates, because the policy for trusted images refuses such an","           image too."," ","-        * portablectl attach now refuses images whose dm-verity signature","-          the host doesn't trust, instead of failing when the service starts.","+        * By default, the image policies that portablectl attach and reattach","+          generate only pin the file system type of each partition, the","+          partition flags and which data partitions exist. The new","+          --pin-protection=yes option also pins the dm-verity protection and","+          the signature of the attached images, as before. With","+          --pin-protection=yes, portablectl attach refuses images whose","+          dm-verity signature the host doesn't trust, instead of failing when","+          the service starts."," ","         * systemd-networkd and networkctl have been merged into a single","           multi-call binary, with the former becoming a symlink to the latter."],"additions":8,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"man/org.freedesktop.portable1.xml","lines":["@@ -323,12 +323,18 @@ node /org/freedesktop/portable1 {","       the safety checks that ensure the units are not running while the image is attached or detached.","       <varname>SD_SYSTEMD_PORTABLE_FORCE_EXTENSION</varname> will bypass the check that ensures the","       <filename>extension-release.<replaceable>NAME</replaceable></filename> file in the extension image","-      matches the image name. They are defined as follows:</para>","+      matches the image name. For <function>AttachImageWithExtensions()</function> and","+      <function>ReattachImageWithExtensions()</function>, <varname>SD_SYSTEMD_PORTABLE_PIN_PROTECTION</varname>","+      adds the dm-verity protection and the signature of the images to the generated image policies, see","+      the <option>--pin-protection=</option> option of","+      <citerefentry><refentrytitle>portablectl</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>. They","+      are defined as follows:</para>"," ","       <programlisting>"," #define SD_SYSTEMD_PORTABLE_RUNTIME            (UINT64_C(1) &lt;&lt; 0)"," #define SD_SYSTEMD_PORTABLE_FORCE_ATTACH       (UINT64_C(1) &lt;&lt; 1)"," #define SD_SYSTEMD_PORTABLE_FORCE_EXTENSION    (UINT64_C(1) &lt;&lt; 2)","+#define SD_SYSTEMD_PORTABLE_PIN_PROTECTION     (UINT64_C(1) &lt;&lt; 3)"," </programlisting>","     </refsect2>"," "],"additions":7,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"man/portablectl.xml","lines":["@@ -141,13 +141,15 @@","         immediately started (blocking operation unless <option>--no-block</option> is passed) and/or enabled after","         attaching the image.</para>"," ","-        <para>When images are attached, an image policy will be generated that pins the attached image by","-        the exact content that was found while attaching, so that it cannot be swapped downgrading security","-        (e.g.: removing dm-verity protection) without a full reinstallation. For more details on policies, see","-        <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd.image-policy</refentrytitle><manvolnum>7</manvolnum></citerefentry>.","-        If an image contains a dm-verity signature, attaching fails unless a key in the kernel keyring or a","-        certificate in <filename>/etc/verity.d/</filename> (and related directories) validates the","-        signature.</para>","+        <para>When images are attached, <command>portablectl</command> generates an image policy that pins the","+        filesystem type of each partition of the attached image, its partition flags and which data partitions","+        it contains. With","+        <option>--pin-protection=yes</option>, the policy also pins the dm-verity protection and the signature","+        that were found while attaching, so that the image cannot be swapped for one with weaker protection","+        without a full reinstallation. In that case, attaching an image with a dm-verity signature fails unless","+        a key in the kernel keyring or a certificate in <filename>/etc/verity.d/</filename> (and related","+        directories) validates the signature. For more details on policies, see","+        <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd.image-policy</refentrytitle><manvolnum>7</manvolnum></citerefentry>.</para>"," ","         <xi:include href=\"vpick.xml\" xpointer=\"image\"/>","         <xi:include href=\"vpick.xml\" xpointer=\"directory\"/>","@@ -329,6 +331,26 @@","         <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v239\"/></listitem>","       </varlistentry>"," ","+      <varlistentry>","+        <term><option>--pin-protection=<replaceable>BOOL</replaceable></option></term>","+","+        <listitem><para>When attaching or reattaching an image, controls whether the generated","+        <varname>RootImagePolicy=</varname> and <varname>ExtensionImagePolicy=</varname> settings require the","+        dm-verity protection and the signature that the attached images have. Takes a boolean argument.","+        Defaults to no.</para>","+","+        <para>When disabled, the generated policies pin the filesystem type, the partition flags and which","+        data partitions exist, and permit images with any dm-verity protection or signature. Images that","+        contain dm-verity data still use dm-verity. If the host doesn't trust the signature of an image,","+        <command>portablectl</command> attaches the image, and dm-verity checks the image against its root","+        hash without validating the signature. With <option>--user</option>,","+        <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-mountfsd.service</refentrytitle><manvolnum>8</manvolnum></citerefentry>","+        mounts the image and applies its own image policy, which can still require a signature that the host","+        trusts.</para>","+","+        <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v263\"/></listitem>","+      </varlistentry>","+","       <varlistentry>","         <term><option>--copy=</option></term>"," "],"additions":29,"deletions":7,"truncated":false},{"path":"shell-completion/bash/portablectl","lines":["@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@ _portablectl() {","         [STANDALONE]='-q --quiet --runtime --no-reload --cat --no-pager --no-legend","                               --no-ask-password --enable --now -h --help --version","                               --clean --no-block --force --user --system'","-        [ARG]='-p --profile --copy -H --host -M --machine --extension'","+        [ARG]='-p --profile --copy -H --host -M --machine --extension --pin-protection'","     )"," ","     local -A VERBS=(","@@ -56,6 +56,9 @@ _portablectl() {","             --copy)","                 comps=\"copy symlink auto mixed\"","                 ;;","+            --pin-protection)","+                comps=\"yes no\"","+                ;;","             --host|-H)","                 comps=$(compgen -A hostname)","                 ;;"],"additions":4,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/portable/portable.c","lines":["@@ -467,6 +467,7 @@ static int portable_extract_by_path(","                 const char *path,","                 bool path_is_extension,","                 bool relax_extension_release_check,","+                bool pin_protection,","                 char **matches,","                 const ImagePolicy *image_policy,","                 PortableMetadata **ret_os_release,","@@ -633,8 +634,9 @@ static int portable_extract_by_path(","                         if (userns_fd < 0)","                                 return log_debug_errno(userns_fd, \"Failed to allocate user namespace: %m\");"," ","-                        /* Callers only ask for a pinned policy when attaching an image. In that case mountfsd","-                         * sets up Verity with the pinned policy, like we do below in system scope. */","+                        /* Callers only ask for a pinned policy when attaching an image. With","+                         * --pin-protection=yes, mountfsd then sets up Verity with the pinned policy, like we","+                         * do below in system scope. */","                         r = mountfsd_mount_image_fd_full(","                                         /* vl= */ NULL,","                                         rfd,","@@ -643,9 +645,11 @@ static int portable_extract_by_path(","                                         image_policy,","                                         &verity,","                                         flags,","-                                        /* pin_image_policy= */ !!ret_pinned_image_policy,","+                                        /* pin_image_policy= */ ret_pinned_image_policy && pin_protection,","                                         &m,","                                         ret_pinned_image_policy ? &pinned_image_policy : NULL);","+                        if (r >= 0 && pinned_image_policy && !pin_protection)","+                                image_policy_relax_protection(pinned_image_policy);","                 } else {","                         _cleanup_(loop_device_unrefp) LoopDevice *d = NULL;"," ","@@ -690,16 +694,19 @@ static int portable_extract_by_path(","                                 return log_debug_errno(r, \"Failed to guess verity roothash for '%s': %m\", path);"," ","                         /* Callers only ask for a pinned policy when attaching an image. In that case we set","-                         * up Verity with the pinned policy, so that we refuse to attach an image whose","-                         * signature the host doesn't trust, instead of failing when the service starts. We","-                         * also read the metadata through Verity this way. We don't set up Verity when only","-                         * inspecting an image, so that the admin can still inspect an image whose signature","-                         * the host doesn't trust. */","+                         * up Verity with the pinned policy. If the pinned policy requires a signature that the","+                         * host doesn't trust, we refuse to attach the image, instead of failing when the","+                         * service starts. We also read the metadata through Verity this way. We don't set up","+                         * Verity when only inspecting an image, so that the admin can still inspect an image","+                         * whose signature the host doesn't trust. */","                         if (ret_pinned_image_policy) {","                                 pinned_image_policy = image_policy_new_from_dissected(m, &verity);","                                 if (!pinned_image_policy)","                                         return -ENOMEM;"," ","+                                if (!pin_protection)","+                                        image_policy_relax_protection(pinned_image_policy);","+","                                 r = dissected_image_decrypt(","                                                 m,","                                                 /* root= */ NULL,","@@ -824,6 +831,7 @@ static int extract_image_and_extensions(","                 char **extension_image_paths,","                 bool validate_extension,","                 bool relax_extension_release_check,","+                bool pin_protection,","                 const ImagePolicy *image_policy,","                 Image **ret_image,","                 OrderedHashmap **ret_extension_images,","@@ -929,6 +937,7 @@ static int extract_image_and_extensions(","                         image->path,","                         /* path_is_extension= */ false,","                         /* relax_extension_release_check= */ false,","+                        pin_protection,","                         matches,","                         image_policy,","                         &os_release,","@@ -1004,6 +1013,7 @@ static int extract_image_and_extensions(","                                 ext->path,","                                 /* path_is_extension= */ true,","                                 relax_extension_release_check,","+                                pin_protection,","                                 matches,","                                 image_policy,","                                 &extension_release_meta,","@@ -1114,6 +1124,7 @@ int portable_extract(","                         extension_image_paths,","                         /* validate_extension= */ false,","                         /* relax_extension_release_check= */ FLAGS_SET(flags, PORTABLE_FORCE_EXTENSION),","+                        /* pin_protection= */ false,","                         image_policy,","                         &image,","                         &extension_images,","@@ -2101,6 +2112,7 @@ int portable_attach(","                         extension_image_paths,","                         /* validate_extension= */ true,","                         /* relax_extension_release_check= */ FLAGS_SET(flags, PORTABLE_FORCE_EXTENSION),","+                        /* pin_protection= */ FLAGS_SET(flags, PORTABLE_PIN_PROTECTION),","                         image_policy,","                         &image,","                         &extension_images,","@@ -2174,8 +2186,7 @@ int portable_attach(","                 }"," ","         /* When reattaching, we only detach the image after the checks above. If attaching fails these","-         * checks, for example because the host doesn't trust the signature of an image, the image stays","-         * attached. */","+         * checks, for example because no unit files match, the image stays attached. */","         if (FLAGS_SET(flags, PORTABLE_REATTACH)) {","                 _cleanup_strv_free_ char **resolved_extension_paths = NULL;","                 Image *ext;"],"additions":21,"deletions":10,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/portable/portable.h","lines":["@@ -21,11 +21,12 @@ typedef enum PortableFlags {","         PORTABLE_RUNTIME         = 1 << 0, /* Public API via DBUS, do not change */","         PORTABLE_FORCE_ATTACH    = 1 << 1, /* Public API via DBUS, do not change */","         PORTABLE_FORCE_EXTENSION = 1 << 2, /* Public API via DBUS, do not change */","-        PORTABLE_PREFER_COPY     = 1 << 3,","-        PORTABLE_PREFER_SYMLINK  = 1 << 4,","-        PORTABLE_MIXED_COPY_LINK = 1 << 5,","-        PORTABLE_REATTACH        = 1 << 6,","-        _PORTABLE_MASK_PUBLIC    = PORTABLE_RUNTIME | PORTABLE_FORCE_ATTACH | PORTABLE_FORCE_EXTENSION,","+        PORTABLE_PIN_PROTECTION  = 1 << 3, /* Public API via DBUS, do not change */","+        PORTABLE_PREFER_COPY     = 1 << 4,","+        PORTABLE_PREFER_SYMLINK  = 1 << 5,","+        PORTABLE_MIXED_COPY_LINK = 1 << 6,","+        PORTABLE_REATTACH        = 1 << 7,","+        _PORTABLE_MASK_PUBLIC    = PORTABLE_RUNTIME | PORTABLE_FORCE_ATTACH | PORTABLE_FORCE_EXTENSION | PORTABLE_PIN_PROTECTION,","         _PORTABLE_TYPE_MAX,","         _PORTABLE_TYPE_INVALID   = -EINVAL,"," } PortableFlags;"],"additions":6,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/portable/portablectl.c","lines":["@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@ static bool arg_no_block = false;"," static char **arg_extension_images = NULL;"," static bool arg_force = false;"," static bool arg_clean = false;","+static bool arg_pin_protection = false;"," static RuntimeScope arg_runtime_scope = RUNTIME_SCOPE_SYSTEM;"," "," STATIC_DESTRUCTOR_REGISTER(arg_extension_images, strv_freep);","@@ -1271,7 +1272,9 @@ static int attach_reattach_image(int argc, char *argv[], const char *method) {","                 return bus_log_create_error(r);"," ","         if (STR_IN_SET(method, \"AttachImageWithExtensions\", \"ReattachImageWithExtensions\")) {","-                uint64_t flags = (arg_runtime ? PORTABLE_RUNTIME : 0) | (arg_force ? PORTABLE_FORCE_ATTACH | PORTABLE_FORCE_EXTENSION : 0);","+                uint64_t flags = (arg_runtime ? PORTABLE_RUNTIME : 0) |","+                                 (arg_force ? PORTABLE_FORCE_ATTACH | PORTABLE_FORCE_EXTENSION : 0) |","+                                 (arg_pin_protection ? PORTABLE_PIN_PROTECTION : 0);"," ","                 r = sd_bus_message_append(m, \"st\", arg_copy_mode, flags);","         } else","@@ -1301,7 +1304,9 @@ static int attach_reattach_image(int argc, char *argv[], const char *method) {"," VERB(verb_attach_image, \"attach\", \"NAME|PATH [PREFIX…]\\0\", 2, VERB_ANY, 0,","      \"Attach the specified portable service image\");"," static int verb_attach_image(int argc, char *argv[], uintptr_t _data, void *userdata) {","-        return attach_reattach_image(argc, argv, strv_isempty(arg_extension_images) && !arg_force ? \"AttachImage\" : \"AttachImageWithExtensions\");","+        return attach_reattach_image(argc, argv,","+                                     strv_isempty(arg_extension_images) && !arg_force && !arg_pin_protection ?","+                                     \"AttachImage\" : \"AttachImageWithExtensions\");"," }"," "," VERB(verb_detach_image, \"detach\", \"NAME|PATH [PREFIX…]\\0\", 2, VERB_ANY, 0,","@@ -1363,7 +1368,9 @@ static int verb_detach_image(int argc, char *argv[], uintptr_t _data, void *user"," VERB(verb_reattach_image, \"reattach\", \"NAME|PATH [PREFIX…]\\0\", 2, VERB_ANY, 0,","      \"Reattach the specified portable service image\");"," static int verb_reattach_image(int argc, char *argv[], uintptr_t _data, void *userdata) {","-        return attach_reattach_image(argc, argv, strv_isempty(arg_extension_images) && !arg_force ? \"ReattachImage\" : \"ReattachImageWithExtensions\");","+        return attach_reattach_image(argc, argv,","+                                     strv_isempty(arg_extension_images) && !arg_force && !arg_pin_protection ?","+                                     \"ReattachImage\" : \"ReattachImageWithExtensions\");"," }"," "," VERB(verb_is_image_attached, \"is-attached\", \"NAME|PATH\\0\", 2, 2, 0,","@@ -1670,6 +1677,13 @@ static int parse_argv(int argc, char *argv[], char ***remaining_args) {","                         arg_force = true;","                         break;"," ","+                OPTION_LONG(\"pin-protection\", \"BOOL\",","+                            \"Pin dm-verity protection and the signature in the generated image policies\"):","+                        r = parse_boolean_argument(\"--pin-protection=\", opts.arg, &arg_pin_protection);","+                        if (r < 0)","+                                return r;","+                        break;","+","                 OPTION_LONG(\"clean\", NULL,","                             \"When detaching, also remove configuration, state, \"","                             \"cache, logs or runtime data of the portable service(s)\"):"],"additions":17,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/shared/image-policy.c","lines":["@@ -350,6 +350,20 @@ ImagePolicy* image_policy_new_from_dissected(const DissectedImage *image, const","         return image_policy;"," }"," ","+void image_policy_relax_protection(ImagePolicy *p) {","+        assert(p);","+","+        /* Changes a policy from image_policy_new_from_dissected() to allow any Verity protection and","+         * signature for each partition that it pins as verity or signed. The file system types, the other","+         * flags and the absent partitions stay pinned. */","+","+        FOREACH_ARRAY(pp, p->policies, p->n_policies)","+                if (partition_designator_is_verity(pp->designator))","+                        pp->flags = PARTITION_POLICY_OPEN;","+                else if (pp->flags & (PARTITION_POLICY_VERITY|PARTITION_POLICY_SIGNED))","+                        pp->flags |= PARTITION_POLICY_UNPROTECTED|PARTITION_POLICY_VERITY|PARTITION_POLICY_SIGNED;","+}","+"," int image_policy_from_string(const char *s, bool graceful, ImagePolicy **ret) {","         _cleanup_free_ ImagePolicy *p = NULL;","         uint64_t dmask = 0;"],"additions":14,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/shared/image-policy.h","lines":["@@ -115,6 +115,7 @@ int image_policy_intersect(const ImagePolicy *a, const ImagePolicy *b, ImagePoli"," int image_policy_union(const ImagePolicy *a, const ImagePolicy *b, ImagePolicy **ret);"," "," ImagePolicy* image_policy_new_from_dissected(const DissectedImage *image, const VeritySettings *verity);","+void image_policy_relax_protection(ImagePolicy *p);"," ImagePolicy* image_policy_free(ImagePolicy *p);"," "," DEFINE_TRIVIAL_CLEANUP_FUNC(ImagePolicy*, image_policy_free);"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/test/test-image-policy.c","lines":["@@ -712,4 +712,41 @@ TEST(image_policy_new_from_dissected) {","         ASSERT_EQ(policy->policies[PARTITION_USR].flags, (PartitionPolicyFlags) (PARTITION_POLICY_SQUASHFS | PARTITION_POLICY_VERITY | PARTITION_POLICY_GROWFS_OFF | PARTITION_POLICY_READ_ONLY_ON));"," }"," ","+TEST(image_policy_relax_protection) {","+        _cleanup_(image_policy_freep) ImagePolicy *policy = NULL;","+","+        /* image_policy_relax_protection() must allow any Verity protection and signature for a partition","+         * that is pinned as signed, keep its other flags, and open up the verity and signature partitions.","+         * Partitions pinned as absent stay absent. */","+        DissectedImage image = {","+                .verity_sig_ready = true,","+                .partitions = {","+                        [PARTITION_ROOT] = {","+                                .found = true,","+                                .fstype = (char*) \"erofs\",","+                        },","+                        [PARTITION_ROOT_VERITY] = {","+                                .found = true,","+                        },","+                        [PARTITION_ROOT_VERITY_SIG] = {","+                                .found = true,","+                        },","+                },","+        };","+        VeritySettings verity = {","+                .designator = PARTITION_ROOT,","+        };","+","+        policy = image_policy_new_from_dissected(&image, &verity);","+        ASSERT_NOT_NULL(policy);","+        ASSERT_EQ(policy->policies[PARTITION_ROOT].flags, (PartitionPolicyFlags) (PARTITION_POLICY_EROFS | PARTITION_POLICY_SIGNED | PARTITION_POLICY_GROWFS_OFF | PARTITION_POLICY_READ_ONLY_ON));","+        ASSERT_EQ(policy->policies[PARTITION_ROOT_VERITY].flags, (PartitionPolicyFlags) (PARTITION_POLICY_GROWFS_OFF | PARTITION_POLICY_READ_ONLY_ON));","+","+        image_policy_relax_protection(policy);","+        ASSERT_EQ(policy->policies[PARTITION_ROOT].flags, (PartitionPolicyFlags) (PARTITION_POLICY_EROFS | PARTITION_POLICY_VERITY | PARTITION_POLICY_SIGNED | PARTITION_POLICY_UNPROTECTED | PARTITION_POLICY_GROWFS_OFF | PARTITION_POLICY_READ_ONLY_ON));","+        ASSERT_EQ(policy->policies[PARTITION_ROOT_VERITY].flags, (PartitionPolicyFlags) PARTITION_POLICY_OPEN);","+        ASSERT_EQ(policy->policies[PARTITION_ROOT_VERITY_SIG].flags, (PartitionPolicyFlags) PARTITION_POLICY_OPEN);","+        ASSERT_EQ(policy->policies[PARTITION_USR].flags, (PartitionPolicyFlags) PARTITION_POLICY_ABSENT);","+}","+"," DEFINE_TEST_MAIN(LOG_INFO);"],"additions":37,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/units/TEST-29-PORTABLE.image.sh","lines":["@@ -46,27 +46,37 @@ portablectl detach --runtime /run/portables/minimal_7.raw minimal-app0"," test -f /run/portables/minimal_7.raw"," rm /run/portables/minimal_7.raw"," ","-# The host refuses to attach an image whose signature it doesn't trust, so that the service doesn't only","-# fail when it starts. Inspecting the image still works. Without a signature, the same image is attached","-# and pinned to Verity alone.","+# With --pin-protection=yes, the host refuses to attach an image whose signature it doesn't trust, so that","+# the service doesn't only fail when it starts. Inspecting the image s